# Cloudflare Workers Platform Specification

> Boundary: this is an unpinned research snapshot for artifact work, not the
> Edge Canon application contract, a complete current vendor specification, or
> conformance/support evidence. Recheck claims against versioned official
> sources; current target status is generated from the locked registry.

This document records research used to build Cloudflare-target artifacts.

## Platform Overview

**Cloudflare Workers** is a serverless platform that runs code on Cloudflare's global network.

- **Runtime**: V8 JavaScript engine (workerd)
- **Languages**: JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Rust, WebAssembly
- **Network**: 300+ data centers globally
- **Performance**: Sub-10ms cold starts

## Entry Point Format

### Standard Export (Modules Syntax - Recommended)

```javascript
export default {
  async fetch(request, env, ctx) {
    return new Response("Hello World!");
  }
}
```

### Service Worker Syntax (Legacy)

```javascript
addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  event.respondWith(handleRequest(event.request));
});
```

**⚠️ Use modules syntax for all new Workers**

## Handler Parameters

### 1. Request Object

Standard Fetch API Request object:

```typescript
interface Request {
  url: string;           // Full URL
  method: string;        // GET, POST, etc.
  headers: Headers;      // Request headers
  body: ReadableStream;  // Request body
  cf: IncomingRequestCfProperties; // Cloudflare-specific data
}
```

**Special `cf` property:**
```typescript
request.cf.colo         // Data center code
request.cf.country      // ISO country code
request.cf.city         // City name
request.cf.continent    // Continent code
request.cf.timezone     // IANA timezone
```

### 2. Environment Bindings (env)

Access to all configured resources:

```typescript
interface Env {
  // KV Namespaces
  MY_KV: KVNamespace;

  // D1 Databases
  DB: D1Database;

  // R2 Buckets
  BUCKET: R2Bucket;

  // Durable Objects
  MY_DO: DurableObjectNamespace;

  // Environment Variables
  API_KEY: string;

  // Secrets
  SECRET_TOKEN: string;

  // Service Bindings
  AUTH_SERVICE: Fetcher;
}
```

### 3. Execution Context (ctx)

Control request lifecycle:

```typescript
interface ExecutionContext {
  // Wait for async work after response sent
  waitUntil(promise: Promise<any>): void;

  // Pass request through
  passThroughOnException(): void;
}
```

## Response Handling

### Creating Responses

```javascript
// Simple text
new Response("Hello", {
  headers: { "content-type": "text/plain" }
});

// JSON
new Response(JSON.stringify({ message: "Hello" }), {
  headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }
});

// Streaming
new Response(readableStream, {
  headers: { "content-type": "text/event-stream" }
});

// Redirect
Response.redirect("https://example.com", 301);
```

## Storage & Data Services

### KV (Key-Value Storage)

**Use case**: Low-latency, eventually-consistent edge caching

```javascript
// Read
const value = await env.MY_KV.get("key");
const jsonValue = await env.MY_KV.get("key", { type: "json" });

// Write
await env.MY_KV.put("key", "value");
await env.MY_KV.put("key", JSON.stringify(data), {
  expirationTtl: 3600  // 1 hour
});

// Delete
await env.MY_KV.delete("key");

// List keys
const list = await env.MY_KV.list({ prefix: "user:" });
```

**Configuration (wrangler.toml):**
```toml
[[kv_namespaces]]
binding = "MY_KV"
id = "namespace-id"
```

### D1 (SQL Database)

**Use case**: Relational data, SQL queries

```javascript
// Query
const result = await env.DB.prepare(
  "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?"
).bind(userId).first();

// Batch operations
const results = await env.DB.batch([
  env.DB.prepare("INSERT INTO ..."),
  env.DB.prepare("UPDATE ..."),
]);
```

**Configuration:**
```toml
[[d1_databases]]
binding = "DB"
database_name = "my-database"
database_id = "database-id"
```

### R2 (Object Storage)

**Use case**: Large file storage, S3-compatible

```javascript
// Put object
await env.BUCKET.put("file.txt", fileData);

// Get object
const object = await env.BUCKET.get("file.txt");
const text = await object.text();

// Delete
await env.BUCKET.delete("file.txt");

// List objects
const list = await env.BUCKET.list({ prefix: "uploads/" });
```

**Configuration:**
```toml
[[r2_buckets]]
binding = "BUCKET"
bucket_name = "my-bucket"
```

### Durable Objects

**Use case**: Strong consistency, stateful coordination

```javascript
// Get Durable Object stub
const id = env.MY_DO.idFromName("user-123");
const stub = env.MY_DO.get(id);

// Call methods
const response = await stub.fetch(request);
```

## Environment Variables & Secrets

### Environment Variables

Plain text configuration:

```toml
[vars]
ENVIRONMENT = "production"
API_URL = "https://api.example.com"
```

Access:
```javascript
const apiUrl = env.API_URL;
```

### Secrets

Encrypted sensitive data (set via CLI or dashboard):

```bash
wrangler secret put SECRET_TOKEN
```

Access same as env vars:
```javascript
const token = env.SECRET_TOKEN;
```

